 ( 25... Nxd6 { is refuted by the brilliant } 26. Rxd6 $1 Bxd6 27. Bf6 $3 Nc5 ( 27... Nxf6 28. Qg5 Kf8 29. Qxf6 $1 { makes it impossible for Black to avoid mate for long. For example: } Ke8 30. Nxd6 Kd7 31. Bg4 Kc6 32. Nxc4 { and so on. } ) 
28. Qg5 Kf8 29. Nh6 ( 28... Bxd6 28. Rd1 $5 ) 
Ke8 30. Qg8 Bf8 31. Bxf7 Kd7 32. Qg4 { and White’s attack is evidently decisive. } ) 
 ( 25... Rc6 26. Bh6 Qd8 27. Bxf8 Nxf8 28. Nh6 Kg7 29. Nxf7 Qf6 30. d7 { and White wins. } ) 
 { Now back to the main line: } 26. Bd8 $3 Rxd8 27. Rxd6 { The most attractive. But White is also winning after } ( 27. Qg5 Kh8 28. Qxd8 ) 
